# Lick: Hammer-Ons (repertoire plan: st-lick-hammer-on). An original lick in E minor pentatonic,
# open position (E G A B D). Four hammer-ons from open strings: string 4 open to fret 2 (D to E),
# string 3 open to fret 2 (G to A), string 2 open to fret 3 (B to D), string 1 open to fret 3
# (E to G). Pick only the first note of each pair; frets 2 and 3 are fingers 2 and 3.
# The same two-bar phrase climbs one string pair at a time (bars 1-2, 3-4, 5-6), bar 7 runs all
# four hammer-ons in a row, and bar 8 comes home to an E minor chord. Every picked note on a beat
# is a note of Em7 (E G B D); the hammered notes fall between the beats.
title: Lick: Hammer-Ons
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original lick
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: hammer-on, legato, minor pentatonic, lick
tempo: 80
time: 4/4
key: Em

track: Your lick
role: lead
